            <ArticleTitle>Myocardial infarction associated with myocardial bridging: case history and review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>364-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 38-year-old male presented with an acute anterior myocardial infarction. Immediate cardiac catheterization revealed no evidence of angiographically significant atherosclerotic coronary artery disease, but there was a subtotal occlusion of the mid-left anterior descending coronary artery from myocardial muscle bridging. The patient did well with medical management. This review details myocardial bridging and its treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
